What to do:

1. Read the full error message, not just the file/line. It will tell you what type the handler is being assigned to versus what it actually is.

2. Type the handler against the specific element and event it is attached to. For a click handler on a button:

   ```tsx
   const handleClick = (e: React.MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) => {
     // ...
   };
   ```

   For a text input change:

   ```tsx
   const handleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
     // ...
   };
   ```

