  let ignore = false;
  fetchUser(id).then(u => { if (!ignore) setUser(u); });
  return () => { ignore = true; };
}, [id]);
```

**Not a finding here:** `[id]` correctly lists the only reactive value the effect reads, so there's no missing-dependency bug — do not "fix" the dependency array. And there's no index-as-key, mutation, or accessibility/XSS concern in this snippet as written.

